   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to requiring inter-agency\nrecords prepared by an outside consultant at the behest of an agency to be\nsubject to FOIL disclosure",
    "basePrintNo": "S3502",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3502-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §87, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3502\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to requiring\ninter-agency records prepared by an outside consultant at the behest of\nan agency to be subject to FOIL disclosure\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRequires inter-agency records prepared by an outside consultant at the\nbehest of an agency to be subject to FOIL disclosure.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 87 of the public officers law to include\nrecords prepared by an outside consultant at the behest of an agency to\nbe subject to FOIL disclosure.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrently in NYS, when agencies or authorities pay outside consultants\nto do reports, the reports are not subject to FOIL requests (statistics\nor data from those reports are subject).\n\nRecords produced by outside consultants at the behest of an agency are\nused to assist agencies and guide them in making crucial decisions.  It\nis as such important to ensure that these reports are subject to FOIL\ndisclosure.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nSenate\n\n2021-2022: S8925, Referred to Investigations and Government Operations\n\nAssembly\n\n2021-2022: No Assembly Same-As\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
